Subject: [PATCH] fpcmoh: relayout the a921 image message for the matcher

The a921 image message carries the same 24 byte prefix as the a900 but only
11264 bytes of pixels, while the matcher indexes pixels from offset 34. Without
the gap every sample is scored as unusable and enrollment never progresses.

Enable relayout_img_msg for the a921, which opens the 10 byte gap at offset 24
that fpc_img_msg_relayout() has always applied to the a900.

---
libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
@@ -2637,6 +2637,9 @@
       /* patches/0017: one more record per capture than the eleven fixed
        * read states consume; it carries the last 24 bytes of the image. */
       self->read_remaining = TRUE;
+      /* patches/0018: same 24 byte image message prefix as the a900, while the
+       * matcher wants 34. Without the gap every sample is rejected. */
+      self->relayout_img_msg = TRUE;
       break;
 
     case 0xA900:
